
Environment: Production (public demo site)
URL: https://www.saucedemo.com/
Build / Version: index-DnLqFcJI.js
Device: Desktop
OS: Windows 11
Browser: Chrome
User role / Test account: standard_user, then a second user (for example visual_user)

Description
When a user logs out, only the login session is removed. The cart is saved in the browser’s storage, isn’t cleared, and isn’t tied to a user. So when a different user logs in on the same browser, they see the first user’s cart, with the same badge number and products, and can check those products out.

Preconditions
The cart is empty.

Steps to Reproduce
Log in as standard_user.
Add Sauce Labs Backpack and Sauce Labs Bike Light to the cart. The badge shows 2.
Open the menu and click “Logout”.
Log in as a different user, for example visual_user.
Look at the cart badge and open the cart.

Test Data
First user: standard_user
Second user: visual_user
Products: Sauce Labs Backpack, Sauce Labs Bike Light

Actual Result
After logging in as the second user, the badge shows 2.
The cart shows the first user’s products.
The second user can check out the first user’s products.

Expected Result
Logout clears the cart, or each user has their own cart.
A new user who logs in on the same browser starts with an empty cart.

Reproducibility
Always 

Attachment
https://jam.dev/c/a2706d7d-db61-4a7d-bfb3-e209e7fb52ca

Impact
Affects anyone using a shared or public computer.
One user can see what another user planned to buy, which is a privacy issue.
Workaround: Use “Reset App State” before logging out.

Suggested Fix (optional)
Clear “cart-contents” on logout, or save the cart separately for each username.

Acceptance Criteria
Given a user with items in the cart, when they log out, then the cart is cleared.
Given user A logged out with items in the cart, when user B logs in on the same browser, then user B’s cart is empty.
Given the product team decides a cart should be kept after logout, when a user logs back in, then only that user’s own cart is shown [To confirm the wanted behaviour].
